diff --git a/docs/storage-usage.md b/docs/storage-usage.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8a1e816
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/storage-usage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Storage usage
+
+`Account#bytes_used` and `Board#bytes_used` return the latest background-calculated
+number of bytes. Reads use a single indexed total lookup, not an attachment scan.
+An empty account or board returns `0`.
+
+We count original files attached as:
+
+- Card images (`Card#image`).
+- Embeds in board public descriptions (`Board#public_description`).
+- Embeds in card descriptions (`Card#description`).
+- Embeds in comments (`Comment#body`).
+
+Draft and closed cards count too. Avatars, generated variants and previews,
+exports, import archives, unattached uploads, and remote images/videos do not.
+Each attachment counts its blob's `byte_size`: a blob shared between different
+attachment locations counts at each location. Action Text already deduplicates
+repeated references to the same blob within one rich-text field.
+
+A board includes its description, all of its cards, and their comments. An account
+includes all of its boards, regardless of access or publication settings.
+
+## Background processing
+
+Run the `backend` queue and the recurring scheduler. Attachment changes enqueue
+reconciliation immediately; the recurring `reconcile_storage` task also runs every
+minute to backfill existing accounts and recover missed enqueues. Totals are
+**eventually consistent**, so a read immediately after an upload may still return
+the previous total.
+
+Requests mark a per-attachment `Storage::Entry` pending in the attachment's own
+transaction. They do not update a shared account or board counter. A worker reads
+current attachment metadata and compares it to the last accounted board and byte
+size. It processes at most 1,000 entries per transaction, updating board totals,
+the account total, and the checkpoints atomically. It never loads file contents
+or rich-text bodies for accounting.
+
+Workers lock the account's separate `Storage::Total` and pending checkpoints, not
+the Account/Board records used by requests. Queue concurrency controls coalesce
+bursts; database transactions provide correctness even with duplicate workers.
+Concurrent changes remain pending after the current batch, and failed batches
+can be retried without losing or double-counting bytes. There is no global
+attachment-ID watermark that could skip a transaction committing out of order.
+
+Card moves queue a batched refresh of the card's attachments, including comment
+embeds. Reconciliation reads the current board from the database, so delayed jobs
+and multiple moves cannot restore an old board assignment. Removal tracking
+covers destruction, replacement, purge, and both individual and bulk detach.
+
+## Existing data and imports
+
+The first reconciliation of an account backfills its existing attachments in
+batches. To start the periodic sweep manually:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails runner 'Storage::Entry.reconcile_pending_later'
+```
+
+Accounting records are derived data and are not exported. Account imports enqueue
+a fresh scan after their bulk inserts finish. After other deliberate bulk SQL
+changes that bypass model callbacks, enqueue a refresh explicitly:
+
+```ruby
+account.refresh_storage_later
+# Or, for changes confined to one board:
+board.refresh_storage_later
+```
+
+Refreshes scan both existing checkpoints and current attachments in batches, so
+bulk deletions are handled as well as additions. Regular uploads and removals
+only reconcile pending attachments, not the entire account or board.
